### 7. Privacy and sharing behaviour

Clarify will implement a **data compartmentalisation model**, not a security claims model:

- The application stores **two separate data objects** per profile:  
  - `identity` (nickname, relationship, year of birth)  
  - `healthProfile` (all health, lifestyle, family history, questions, gaps, decisions)  
- By default, no identifying detail is attached to any output.  
- On the Take-Forward Pack assembly screen, the user is shown exactly what will be included and can toggle inclusion of the `identity` fields.  
- The application never transmits data to a server. All storage is in the browser’s local storage (or IndexedDB for larger profiles).  
- There is no account, no login and no cloud synchronisation in version one.  
- The export PDF is generated entirely client-side; no data leaves the device.  
- The interface does not describe the system as “secure”, “encrypted” or “protected”; it simply states: “Your information is stored only on this device and is not sent anywhere unless you choose to print or save a copy.”

